From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexandre Derumier <aderumier@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] winedmo: Let the demuxer read while it seeks.

media_source_start() sets read_flushing to cut short the demux thread's
read, then seeks the demuxer with it still set: every read the demuxer
makes while it seeks returns no data. ffmpeg's ASF demuxer finds its seek
point by reading packets, so after a seek it resumed in the middle of a
packet and dropped the keyframe ("packet fragment position invalid",
"first frame is no keyframe"); the frames after it were decoded on an
empty reference, grey and black blocks until the next keyframe.

Hoshi to Tsubasa no Paradox (Unreal Engine 4 WmfMedia) seeks its movies
while they play; CP_HUD_v6.wmv (WMV3, its only keyframe the first frame)
stayed garbled to its end.

The demux thread reads with demuxer_cs held and does not read again while
flushing is set: clear read_flushing once the seek holds demuxer_cs.
---
--- a/dlls/winedmo/media_source.c
+++ b/dlls/winedmo/media_source.c
@@ -923,11 +923,16 @@
 
         WARN("MF media source seek to %s.\n", debugstr_time(position->hVal.QuadPart));
         EnterCriticalSection(&source->demuxer_cs);
+        /* read_flushing cut short the demux thread's read; it is done with
+         * demuxer_cs held and flushing keeps it from reading again: the
+         * demuxer's own reads while it seeks must get their data (ASF finds
+         * its seek point by reading packets: empty reads made it resume in
+         * the middle of a packet, without the keyframe). */
+        source->read_flushing = FALSE;
         winedmo_demuxer_seek(source->demuxer, position->hVal.QuadPart);
         LeaveCriticalSection(&source->demuxer_cs);
 
         source->flushing = FALSE;
-        source->read_flushing = FALSE;
     }
 
     for (i = 0; i < source->stream_count; i++)
